bootstrap: vendor and generate-copyright scan the workspaces the tree carries

Why a patch: default_paths_to_vendor lists every cargo workspace of the
monorepo, including the documentation books (src/tools/rustbook with
src/doc/book and src/doc/reference, src/doc/book/packages/trpl) and
src/tools/rustc-perf, which are git submodules. DevTools' source tree is
the release at the pin with the submodules the build needs (cargo,
backtrace) and nothing else (D-0003, D-0006), marked as a release source
with git-commit-info; generate-copyright, run by dist::Rustc for the
COPYRIGHT files, runs `cargo metadata` over that whole list and fails on
the first workspace that is not there. This keeps only the workspaces
whose manifest exists and whose required submodules are checked out, so
the COPYRIGHT files cover what is actually built. Nothing of what the
compiler emits changes. Written by EmiBSD (ISC); carried by DevTools over
the pinned tag, offered upstream when stable. Author: Emilio Navarrete
Lineros, 2026-10-31.

--- a/src/bootstrap/src/core/build_steps/vendor.rs
+++ b/src/bootstrap/src/core/build_steps/vendor.rs
@@ -33,6 +33,12 @@
     ]
     .into_iter()
     .map(|(path, submodules)| (builder.src.join(path), submodules))
+    // Only the workspaces this tree carries: a release source may leave out the
+    // submodules the build does not need (the documentation books, rustc-perf).
+    .filter(|(path, submodules)| {
+        path.exists()
+            && submodules.iter().all(|s| !crate::utils::helpers::dir_is_empty(&builder.src.join(s)))
+    })
     .collect()
 }
 
